From: Alex <75579937+AlexandreL04@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:26:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] qwen35: calibration statistics for quantizers
 (TQLLM_CALIB_OUT)

With TQLLM_CALIB_OUT=FILE the engine accumulates, for each matmul input
of the trunk, the sum over prefilled tokens of x x^T restricted to every
128-wide block, in the rotated basis the TQ weights are stored in, and
rewrites FILE after every prefilled prompt. A quantizer can use it as
the per-block Hessian of its rounding error. Prefill chunks only, one
slot; without the variable nothing is allocated or computed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EcABmjDqBccKS6zFKBPTCA
---
 src/models/qwen/qwen35/qwen35_engine.hpp  | 16 ++++++
 src/models/qwen/qwen35/qwen35_forward.cpp | 61 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/models/qwen/qwen35/qwen35_spec.cpp    |  3 ++
 3 files changed, 80 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/models/qwen/qwen35/qwen35_engine.hpp b/src/models/qwen/qwen35/qwen35_engine.hpp
index af6dd13..49a782a 100644
--- a/src/models/qwen/qwen35/qwen35_engine.hpp
+++ b/src/models/qwen/qwen35/qwen35_engine.hpp
@@ -136,6 +136,10 @@ public:
             smooth_prebuild();
             memlog("calibrate");
             pc_on = opt.prompt_cache || (kv_cmp && slots == 1);  // several slots: each keeps its own conversation
+            if (const char * e = std::getenv("TQLLM_CALIB_OUT"); e && *e) {
